WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.677
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:04.977 --> 00:00:08.259
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:14.682
Unit twenty-two: Arts and Entertainment. In this unit, you will describe shows, art and how they make you feel.

4
00:00:15.683 --> 00:00:16.638
fascinating.

5
00:00:17.338 --> 00:00:19.523
fascinating means extremely interesting.

6
00:00:19.823 --> 00:00:22.612
The documentary about the Mekong was fascinating.

7
00:00:23.312 --> 00:00:25.941
Your turn. Say: fascinating.

8
00:00:28.641 --> 00:00:29.735
fascinating.

9
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:31.809
performance.

10
00:00:32.509 --> 00:00:36.564
performance means a show in which people act, sing, dance or play music.

11
00:00:36.864 --> 00:00:39.095
The dancers gave a beautiful performance.

12
00:00:39.795 --> 00:00:42.343
Your turn. Say: performance.

13
00:00:45.043 --> 00:00:46.091
performance.

14
00:00:47.083 --> 00:00:47.701
critic.

15
00:00:48.401 --> 00:00:52.804
critic means a person who writes their opinion about films, books or art.

16
00:00:53.104 --> 00:00:55.301
The critic gave the film five stars.

17
00:00:56.001 --> 00:00:58.398
Your turn. Say: critic.

18
00:01:01.098 --> 00:01:01.960
critic.

19
00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:03.905
stage play.

20
00:01:04.605 --> 00:01:07.997
stage play means a story performed by actors in a theatre.

21
00:01:08.297 --> 00:01:10.808
We saw a stage play about the Khmer Empire.

22
00:01:11.508 --> 00:01:14.067
Your turn. Say: stage play.

23
00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:17.745
stage play.

24
00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:19.937
box office hit.

25
00:01:20.637 --> 00:01:23.356
box office hit means a film that makes a lot of money.

26
00:01:23.656 --> 00:01:26.167
The new Khmer horror film was a box office hit.

27
00:01:26.867 --> 00:01:29.728
Your turn. Say: box office hit.

28
00:01:32.428 --> 00:01:33.766
box office hit.

29
00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:35.542
talented.

30
00:01:36.242 --> 00:01:39.461
talented means having a natural ability to do something well.

31
00:01:39.761 --> 00:01:41.342
She is a talented young singer.

32
00:01:42.042 --> 00:01:45.031
Your turn. Say: talented.

33
00:01:47.731 --> 00:01:48.686
talented.

34
00:01:49.683 --> 00:01:50.452
moving.

35
00:01:51.152 --> 00:01:54.719
moving means making you feel strong emotions, often sadness.

36
00:01:55.019 --> 00:01:57.042
The ending of the film was very moving.

37
00:01:57.742 --> 00:01:59.918
Your turn. Say: moving.

38
00:02:02.618 --> 00:02:03.445
moving.

39
00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:05.161
premiere.

40
00:02:05.861 --> 00:02:08.754
premiere means the first public showing of a film or play.

41
00:02:09.054 --> 00:02:11.472
The actors attended the premiere in Phnom Penh.

42
00:02:12.172 --> 00:02:14.279
Your turn. Say: premiere.

43
00:02:16.979 --> 00:02:17.829
premiere.

44
00:02:18.817 --> 00:02:20.921
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:21.221 --> 00:02:23.998
Did you see the new stage play at the national theatre?

46
00:02:25.283 --> 00:02:28.937
Yes! The performance was amazing. I was really moved.

47
00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.308
I heard the ending was very moving.

48
00:02:33.617 --> 00:02:37.500
It was. But the first hour was a bit boring, to be honest.

49
00:02:38.783 --> 00:02:41.642
The critic said the actors were extremely talented.

50
00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:46.009
I agree. I was fascinated by the costumes too.

51
00:02:47.317 --> 00:02:50.663
Grammar focus: -ed and -ing adjectives.

52
00:02:50.963 --> 00:02:54.054
Use -ing adjectives to describe the thing or situation.

53
00:02:54.354 --> 00:02:57.456
Use -ed adjectives to describe how a person feels.

54
00:02:57.756 --> 00:03:01.196
For example: The film was boring, so I was bored.

55
00:03:01.496 --> 00:03:05.202
Be careful: 'I am boring' means other people find you boring!

56
00:03:06.217 --> 00:03:09.090
Now read and listen. A Golden Age for Khmer Film.

57
00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:13.839
In the 1960s, Cambodia had a very exciting film industry.

58
00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:18.102
Talented directors made hundreds of films every year.

59
00:03:19.417 --> 00:03:22.182
Sadly, most of these films were lost during the war.

60
00:03:23.483 --> 00:03:27.561
Today, a new generation of filmmakers is creating moving stories again.

61
00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:32.115
Several Khmer films have been shown at international premieres.

62
00:03:33.417 --> 00:03:35.883
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:36.183 --> 00:03:38.125
Extremely interesting means blank.

64
00:03:38.425 --> 00:03:41.939
A, fascinating. B, talented. C, moving.

65
00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.054
The answer is A: fascinating.

66
00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:52.655
The lesson was very blank. I almost fell asleep.

67
00:03:52.955 --> 00:03:55.657
A, bored. B, boring. C, bore.

68
00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:01.197
The answer is B: boring.

69
00:04:02.683 --> 00:04:04.741
I was blank by the beautiful music.

70
00:04:05.041 --> 00:04:08.056
A, moving. B, moved. C, move.

71
00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:13.504
The answer is B: moved.

72
00:04:15.017 --> 00:04:17.353
A film that makes a lot of money is a blank.

73
00:04:17.653 --> 00:04:22.015
A, stage play. B, box office hit. C, performance.

74
00:04:26.017 --> 00:04:28.156
The answer is B: box office hit.

75
00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:33.519
According to the text, when did Cambodia have an exciting film industry?

76
00:04:33.819 --> 00:04:39.725
A, in the 1960s. B, in the 1990s. C, in the 2010s.

77
00:04:43.717 --> 00:04:46.506
The answer is A: in the 1960s.

78
00:04:48.017 --> 00:04:52.480
Now it's your turn to speak. Describe a film, show or concert that you found exciting.

79
00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:02.929
The concert last year was amazing. I was so excited when my favourite band came on stage.

80
00:05:03.229 --> 00:05:04.996
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:05.983 --> 00:05:09.727
Great work today! You learned eight new words and -ed and -ing adjectives.

82
00:05:10.027 --> 00:05:13.898
Today's value is creativity. Use your imagination when you play.

83
00:05:14.198 --> 00:05:17.118
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

84
00:05:17.418 --> 00:05:20.047
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

